zotero-translate-files-pref-request-help = The plugin packs a whole document into as few requests as possible. Output is estimated at 1.6× source tokens plus 20 tokens per paragraph, with 10% headroom. After truncation, the last item is treated as unconfirmed and resent with the remaining suffix; a batch is split in half only when no complete items are confirmed. Every actual API request counts. Failed paragraphs can be repaired together after the main pass; repair requests count against the limit. References are kept in the source language by default. Chatanywhere has a hard cap of 100 requests per document, so keep this limit lower to preserve quota. Automatic glossary extraction and per-paragraph fallback requests are disabled.
zotero-translate-files-pref-babeldoc-help = Install BabelDOC with scripts/install-babeldoc.ps1. After installation, copy the default path printed by the script; enter either babeldoc.exe or the environment's python.exe.
